    "answer": {
      "short": "He calculated quantity per cost, so he should choose the higher value. The 500 g pack for \\$1.95 is better value.",
      "worked": "Mario calculated $\\frac{\\text{quantity}}{\\text{cost}}$ in grams per cent. A higher value means more pasta for each cent.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{First pack quantity per cent}&=\\frac{200}{80}\\text{ g}\\\\&=2.5\\text{ g}\\\\\\text{Second pack quantity per cent}&=\\frac{500}{195}\\text{ g}\\\\&=\\frac{100}{39}\\text{ g}\\\\&=2.564102\\ldots\\text{ g}\\end{align*}$$\nThe second rate is higher, so 500 g for \\$1.95 is better value.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
